# Intent: Train 2 item 9, quiet reconnect and the offline tone after 3 minutes (rebuild of the old 119, 120 and the quiet half of 141). Every failed reconnect to Home raised an error event that played the exclamation tone and drew the error face, so a Home restart (30 to 60 s, several a day while Home installs) chimed every few seconds. Now the error is only logged. The unit plays one offline tone when the link has been down for 3 minutes (a real outage), through the sound policy so it is silent at night and when muted, and a "back" chime only after a tone that sounded; a restart that ends sooner makes no sound at all. No tone while Home has not approved the unit (a setup state with its own look). The offline tone is the shipped tap tone (the asset set has no separate offline sound). The pure rule is maipai_link_quiet_core.h; the websocket reconnect task calls down, poll and up. Skipped, with the reason: the old 151 "charged once per session" cue, because this image has no plug-in or charged tone (the policy answers "missing" for them) and nothing reads the charger events, so there is no cue to limit.
